{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqar2syv6m2","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"wiring duty belongs to dispatcher tier not worker agents","summary":"User decision (2026-06-12): graph wiring (suggest_links + add_dependency at task creation) is the DISPATCHER's job, done BEFORE dispatch — never delegated to worker subagents. Why: workers reliably drop unenforced protocol steps (wiring has no gate, unlike start_task); small models can't judge suggest_links noise; workers lack the structural context (e.g. file-collision blocking edges). Workers keep exactly two graph duties: start_task before writes (gate-enforced) and complete_task with summary; plus wires_to on any record_decision they make mid-task. Dispatcher prompts must contain the claim contract verbatim (exact task_key, agent_id, ToolSearch query).","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T09:54:53.095Z","vec":[-0.11752863228321075,-0.03153974935412407,-0.018695803359150887,0.029853137210011482,-0.06199683994054794,0.04043620824813843,0.024564893916249275,-0.022846687585115433,-0.061523985117673874,0.0034547187387943268,0.028165778145194054,-0.0745735689997673,0.002733404515311122,0.05273614823818207,0.03903140500187874,0.06765713542699814,0.11272559314966202,-0.025470824912190437,0.018521150574088097,-0.07332565635442734,0.06038729101419449,-0.027268726378679276,-0.059459105134010315,0.009328224696218967,0.010178327560424805,-0.022672777995467186,-0.0632079467177391,0.029402930289506912,-0.014155673794448376,-0.00860880222171545,-0.039523981511592865,0.009805235080420971,-0.047613006085157394,-0.004788069985806942,0.023403886705636978,0.08614980429410934,0.03236737102270126,-0.003180376486852765,0.12698282301425934,0.020982814952731133,0.04990675672888756,0.00026268334477208555,-0.052929360419511795,-0.05555974319577217,-0.08458156883716583,-0.023271242156624794,0.06396938860416412,-0.03950268402695656,-0.011015771888196468,-0.004075710196048021,-0.017051061615347862,0.029935624450445175,0.0